  "obligation": "Passive data availability/drop lifecycle, active segments starting dropped, and Memory32 bulk initialization/copy/fill through the shared VM, including overlapping and cross-memory copies, exact bounds and independent instance ownership.",
  "representation": "WasmDataMode owns static active/passive mode. Immutable Rc byte facts are shared; each instance Environment owns an immutable segment backing handle or Undefined as the dropped state after global and memory slots. DataDrop lowers to LoadConst/StoreCapture. Three new bulk opcode rows reuse RegisterPair layout, residual validation/disassembly/liveness, and the existing dispatch loop. MemoryInit and MemoryCopy share checked byte-copy effects; MemoryFill shares the range authority. Both copy ranges are checked before writing; same-memory copy_within preserves overlap semantics. Mutable backing has one detached/immutable guard. Residual format is 48.",
